WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.604 line:0%
Gav:<i> Today we are
 on the Illinois River.</i>

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.372 align:start position:0% line:0%
Anyone die
doing this before?

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:08.775 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
Nobody's ever been killed.
Just a few broken jaws.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.676 align:start position:0% line:0%
Oh, joy.

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:14.680 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is one of the most
mental things I've ever filmed.

00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:17.650
Gav:<i> Dan, we got, like,
 15 fish in the air.</i>

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.685
Whoa! Flippin'-A!

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.821 align:start position:0%
This is chaos.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.524
Whoa, whoa! Oof!

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.559 size:81% position:41%
That is one of my favorite
things we've ever filmed.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.766 align:start position:0% line:0%
Well, wasn't that
a lovely day on the river?

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:37.336 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
Well, I mean, for you.
You just sat on a boat
having a nice day.

00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:40.139 align:start size:78% position:22%
I was holding on
for dear life getting hit
in the face with fish.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.508 align:start position:0%
- Getting pelted. My ideal day.
- Oh, fine, yeah.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:45.578 align:start size:97% position:3%
- No, it was quite fun.
- My favorite clip, I think--

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:47.113
I think the one of you
getting hit in the face.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.347
Whoa, whoa! Oof!

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.516 align:start size:75% position:25%
- ( Gav laughs )
- Jesus.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:52.618 align:start position:0%
We honestly
couldn't have asked
for a more perfect shot

00:00:52.651 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start position:0%
- That's true.
- than that one that just
  beaned you right in the head.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.788 align:start size:78% position:22%
- Yeah.
- And that is one
  of my favorites.

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:58.091
I also very much like
this shot.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.459
<i> Something I noticed,</i>

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.360
<i> and you can see it
 if I zoom in,</i>

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:03.696
<i> as the fish lands
 on your life jacket,</i>

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.364
<i> a little bit of poo.</i>

00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:06.766
<i> That is fish poo
 coming out of there.</i>

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.868
Dan:<i> It left a smear.
 It left a smear.</i>

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.636
<i> I wondered why I was getting
 covered in stuff.</i>

00:01:10.669 --> 00:01:12.338
<i> I've never been pooed on
 by a fish.</i>

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:13.773 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well, it's all well and good
being hit in the face

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.175 align:start position:0%
- with flying fish and pooed on.
- Well, it looks cool.

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:17.643 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Yeah.
- But why are they jumping
  out of the water?

00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:20.213 align:start size:75% position:25%
To find out, we spoke
to a bloke called Jason.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.648 align:start position:0%
So we might as well
start with the basics.
What makes these fish jump?

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.117 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
Well, there's a variety

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:75% position:25% line:0%
of different things
that can make fish jump.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.520
<i> These fish are more
 than likely jumping</i>

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.188
<i> to try and avoid what they
perceive as a predation threat,</i>

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:30.523
<i> something trying to eat them.</i>

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.758
<i> What's actually causing
 them to respond</i>

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.427
<i> is the sound
 and pressure waves</i>

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.728
<i> that are coming off
 the hull of the boat</i>

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:37.730 align:start size:56% position:44%
and, specifically,
the boat motor.

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.398 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Interesting.
- So the fish weren't
  always here.

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:41.567
They're not native to America.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.870
They're called Asian carp.
How did they actually
get here then?

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:47.273 size:78% position:61%
They were intentionally
introduced into southern
United States fish farms.

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:50.143 align:start size:88% position:13%
As those ponds were drained,
some of the carp escaped.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.645
<i> Anything that's connected
to the lower Mississippi River,</i>

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.248
<i> which is one
 of the largest rivers
 in the western hemisphere,</i>

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.749
<i> they're branching out
 and expanding.</i>

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.818
So what's the worst thing
about them?

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
- What kind of damage
  do they do?
- From a social standpoint,

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.389 align:start size:50% position:50%
they worst thing
they do is jump.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.658 align:start size:78% position:22%
People have been injured,
when a 6 to 16-pound fish

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:07.260 align:start size:53% position:47%
comes crashing
into your person.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.561
Yeah.

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:10.630 align:start position:0%
( grunts, groans )

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.632 align:start size:72% position:28%
The ecological problems
that they cause

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.500 align:start size:59% position:41%
have a lot of us
ecologists worried.

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:17.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
They eat plankton and other
microscopic plants and animals

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:18.704 align:start size:72% position:28%
that most of the fish
in the river depend on.

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:20.273
Right, so they're just, like--

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.542 align:start position:0%
they're nipping other fish
in the bud before--

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.711
The worst case scenario is that
they keep spreading unchecked.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:28.514 align:start position:0%
So what can we do as humans
to maybe start fixing
this problem?

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:31.918 align:start size:75% position:25%
The easiest thing to do
and the best thing to do
is actually to eat them.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.387 align:start size:66% position:34%
They taste good,
they're good for you,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.389 align:start size:72% position:28%
and you don't even have
to be a good angler
to catch them.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.191 align:start size:72% position:28%
They jump in your boat.
They volunteer.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.526 align:start position:0%
- It's really the perfect fish.
- Wait, so they taste good,

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:42.295 align:start size:97% position:3%
- they volunteer to be eaten.
- Yeah.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.796
You just need
to change the name.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start position:0%
Just give it
a more glamorous name,
like a yum fish.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.934 align:start position:0%
Dan:
Yummy, yummy fish.
That's it.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.802 align:start position:0%
All right, thanks very much,
Jason. Very informative.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.804
- My pleasure. Thank you.
- Thank you very much.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:53.873 align:start size:88% position:13%
All right,
back to you Gav and Dan.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:56.475 align:start position:0%
Thanks, us.
Well, you heard what he said.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:57.910 align:start position:0%
More people have got
to start eating these fish.

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.912 align:start size:72% position:28%
Obviously, I thought
we'd do it our own way,

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:03.382 align:start size:63% position:38%
so I thought
we'd slow cook them.

00:03:03.415 --> 00:03:04.684 align:start size:81% position:19%
- I like what
  you've done there.
- Thank you.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.985
Very clever.

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start position:0%
Here, we gotta chef up.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.657 size:81% position:41%
So while Dan is preparing
this delicious Asian carp,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.961 align:start position:0%
why don't we take a lovely
slo-mo look at how we caught it?

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:18.298
- All right, rolling again.
- All right, here we go.

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:27.707
Whoa!

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:36.583 align:start position:0%
Gav:
That was a good attempt.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:43.723
( Gav laughs )

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.926
Gav:<i> But you bend down here.</i>

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:48.527
Dan:<i> You see, I was losing
 my balance slightly</i>

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.363
<i> 'cause I had to--</i>

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.233
Gav:<i> And it just shot
 straight from the middle.</i>

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Dan:<i> Getting my balance. </i>
-<i> Oof.</i>

00:03:56.902 --> 00:03:58.604
 Gav:<i> But the moment
 I saw it hit you,</i>

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:01.374
<i> I zoomed in for the reaction.
 It just...</i>

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.775
Dan:
<i> Square on the face.</i>

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:04.877
 Gav:<i> ...absolutely
 wiped you there.</i>

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.546
Dan:<i> It was fine, actually.
 The helmet worked.</i>

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:10.883
<i> That, like,
 proper wiped me out.</i>

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.752
<i> I was just gone there.</i>

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.687
Gav:<i> Very nice.</i>

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.723 size:84% position:58%
All right, if you scoop one
out of the air with a net,

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:19.659 align:start size:81% position:19%
- that's 150 points.
- That'd be boss.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.694 align:start size:66% position:34%
Yeah. All right,
let's get back on.

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:24.998 align:start size:16% position:84%
Whoa!

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.304 align:start size:50% position:50%
Whoa! Whoa!

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.510
- ( grunts ) Yeah!
- Oh, he got it!

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:38.878
- He's got it!
- I got him.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.313 align:start size:44% position:56%
Got a big one.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.948
<i> ( classical music playing )</i>

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:10.643
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:17.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you get off your phone
while we're at dinner, please?

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:20.086 align:start position:0%
Sorry.
I'm gonna go for the lemon.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:22.388 align:start position:0%
Oh, God.

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:24.390 align:start size:59% position:41%
That's pretty good.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:27.093 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Let's have a taste.
- Solid.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.494 align:start position:0%
Tastes like fish.

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:29.995 align:start size:78% position:22%
